LRC14 CIRCUIT-COMPLEXITY PAST-WORK SYNTHESIS
status: evidence / executable synthesis; not a proof
vertex_set: proof carriers and sidecar gates, not runners or arcs
pairwise_observable: retained LRC predicate, exact gap readout, uniform family, route purity, sidecar closure, bridge safety, proof readiness, destroyed-coordinate discharge, and finite-bank warning
switch: majority comparison of the observable vector; ties use weighted payload then the declared tie path
tie_hamiltonian_path:
  endpoint_phi_relu_gap -> endpoint_cover_circuit_positivity -> automatic_magnitude_zipper -> route_state_horn_median_hull -> protected_branch_graph_no_naked_bridge -> pde_weak_form_endpoint_compiler -> mciq_monotone_proof_frontier -> three_state_middle_automaton -> finite_bank_apex_threshold_warning -> raw_scalar_p0_shadow

PAST-WORK FACTS
- HYP-2112: Phi(C)=mu(safe set) verified exactly 900/900 for n=6..14; Phi>0 iff loose.
- HYP-2108: P(S)>0 iff loose for endpoint-cover circuits; sign gate precedes Phi value.
- HYP-2109: L/M/R automaton proposes M as the unavoidable wall/tie corridor.
- HYP-3016: Automatic/residue languages mix AP/GW boundary atoms with open rows unless magnitude is retained.
- HYP-3023: Full HYP-2963 bank: magnitude_cocycle has 100.0% route purity after automatic fibers mix.
- HYP-3077: Horn proof-state hull: 41 features, 34 rules, 29791 triples, 0 illegal centers.
- HYP-3082: Raw scalar star has 5 naked bridges; protected branch graph has 0 naked bridges.
- HYP-3111: Monotone proof-frontier circuit has 10 inputs, size 8, depth 4, all inputs essential.
- HYP-3115: Finite-bank literal apex7_error<=5 isolates max p0, but is explicitly a uniformity warning.

CARRIER LEDGER
- endpoint_phi_relu_gap
  sources: HYP-2112, HYP-2108
  role: exact numeric output gate
  payload_score: 108
  circuit_proxy: size=4, depth=2
  retains: Phi(C)=mu(safe set) as a ReLU/ramp gap sum
  destroys_or_warns: which endpoint owners caused each ramp unless paired with HYP-2108
  next_test: compile Phi, endpoint owners, and multiple-of-14 checks into HYP-2963 rows
- endpoint_cover_circuit_positivity
  sources: HYP-2108
  role: closed endpoint-cover sign gate
  payload_score: 97
  circuit_proxy: size=3, depth=2
  retains: P(S)>0 iff loose; midpoint circuit resonance
  destroys_or_warns: gap magnitude; recovered by HYP-2112 Phi
  next_test: pair P-sign with Phi-value so tight/worry kernels become explicit proof obligations
- three_state_middle_automaton
  sources: HYP-2109
  role: stateful wall-crossing gate
  payload_score: 81
  circuit_proxy: size=3, depth=2
  retains: L/M/R terminal state, with M as wall or tie corridor
  destroys_or_warns: metric gap size and magnitude cocycle
  next_test: prove or refute no-closed-middle around endpoint-cover circuits
- automatic_magnitude_zipper
  sources: HYP-3016, HYP-3023
  role: finite-state quotient repaired by magnitude cocycle
  payload_score: 104
  circuit_proxy: size=6, depth=3
  retains: (M, q_threshold, farey_excess, lacunary_tail_ratio)
  destroys_or_warns: route purity inside automatic/residue-terminal fibers
  next_test: turn the magnitude cocycle purity into a family lemma for automatic fibers
- route_state_horn_median_hull
  sources: HYP-3074, HYP-3077
  role: proof-circuit legality and closure gate
  payload_score: 107
  circuit_proxy: size=34, depth=2
  retains: packet/route/certificate/sidecar/discharge Horn closure
  destroys_or_warns: specific terminal atom when only scheduler center survives
  next_test: compile multi-premise sidecar laws or prove the current unary closure is enough
- protected_branch_graph_no_naked_bridge
  sources: HYP-3082
  role: terminal no-naked-bridge gate
  payload_score: 113
  circuit_proxy: size=83, depth=4
  retains: protected branch graph after route/section/grid/no-lift/q-cusp exits
  destroys_or_warns: raw scalar-star bridges; five naked bridges before protection
  next_test: prove every primitive residual emits the protected sidecar set before contraction
- mciq_monotone_proof_frontier
  sources: HYP-3111, HYP-3115
  role: bounded monotone proof-circuit frontier
  payload_score: 92
  circuit_proxy: size=8, depth=4
  retains: 10-input monotone proof-frontier circuit, size 8, depth 4
  destroys_or_warns: uniform family parameter and non-fitted thresholds
  next_test: replace finite-bank literals with a uniform circuit over named proof sidecars
- pde_weak_form_endpoint_compiler
  sources: HYP-3111, HYP-2112, HYP-2108
  role: weak-form compiler into endpoint Phi
  payload_score: 99
  circuit_proxy: size=8, depth=5
  retains: mass/stiffness/boundary/zero-mode data routed to Phi
  destroys_or_warns: root/free-energy geometry before the weak-form packet is typed
  next_test: annotate residual rows with mass, stiffness, zero modes, Phi, and terminal exit
- finite_bank_apex_threshold_warning
  sources: HYP-3115
  role: small fitted classifier warning
  payload_score: 21
  circuit_proxy: size=1, depth=1
  retains: single bounded-bank literal apex7_error <= 5
  destroys_or_warns: uniformity, proof basis, and reason the threshold is not fitted
  next_test: use only as an alarm that a genuine uniform circuit field is missing
- raw_scalar_p0_shadow
  sources: HYP-3103, HYP-3115
  role: negative-control scalar output
  payload_score: 6
  circuit_proxy: size=1, depth=1
  retains: single value p0=G(0)
  destroys_or_warns: root locus, route label, endpoint owners, and all proof sidecars
  next_test: never use without a retained root/ear/gap/route certificate

